---
Fix ftell() error handling.

ftell() can return -1L on error, but current code uses the return value
without checking, leading to incorrect file size calculations or
underflow when cast to unsigned.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All ftell() calls check for -1L return value
- [ ] On ftell failure: log error, close file, return error code
- [ ] No unsigned cast of unchecked ftell return value
- [ ] Applies to sample_io.c, project.c, and any other file I/O

## Test Plan
- [ ] Audit all ftell() calls in codebase
- [ ] Test with unreadable file (permissions), verify graceful error
- [ ] Verify no negative-to-unsigned conversion warnings with -Wsign-conversion
